id #uuid "12d5f996-d678-561d-9aeb-56f00bf63bd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571571} {:answer/id #uuid "3544a24c-4c09-5a19-8d86-feae12696232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571629} {:answer/id #uuid "3e28e280-488e-5791-b37f-8856d5bc48c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571655} {:answer/id #uuid "439f7774-9836-5a9c-9f14-7f34676f9df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571660} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc6c962-5504-597b-91bc-f1de44797a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571726}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571571} :answer-field/id #uuid "3503b61a-03e7-59f3-bf35-78da79a64edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a23203af-cedc-5b8e-8d72-0b2828db1bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-39068" :question/problem "What is the index of the term $\\frac{79}{2}$ for the arithmetic sequence below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+1,\\,{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2},\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will convert the recursive formula to an explicit formula and then solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=\\frac{79}{2}.$\n\nThe recursive rule for an arithmetic sequence takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d.\n$$\n\nIn the given formula, we have $d=1.$ We are also told that ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2},$ so we can write the explicit formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(n-1)(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+n-1 \\\\  & =n-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=\\frac{79}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =n-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{79}{2} & =n-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{79}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =n \\\\ 40 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{79}{2}$ is the $40$th term of the sequence."} :step/id #uuid "3dba212a-9eb2-52b3-9f03-fa81d6520f9b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572218}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572264 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f5ccb9-bad9-5bda-8ffd-bf405fd74bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571543} {:answer/id #uuid "1b13c477-4b05-5b3b-b27b-a59b3642e251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571585} {:answer/id #uuid "3613780e-0f33-54fd-b742-695b4b426da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571633} {:answer/id #uuid "3816d746-55ba-50dc-9a6d-a9bfb5504358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571639} {:answer/id #uuid "d78889bb-fcaa-54ed-a419-ab7b588b2cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571927}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571585} :answer-field/id #uuid "242366b2-7b20-5372-baa3-2e53989791c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "793b000c-58a2-555d-902b-eb4a4369fd1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-101063" :question/problem "Given an arithmetic sequence that has ${a}_{3}=-5$ and common difference $d=2,$ what is the index of the term $99?$" :question/worked-solution "Since ${a}_{3}=-5$ is $2$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}+2d \\\\ -5 & ={a}_{1}+2(2) \\\\ -5 & ={a}_{1}+4 \\\\ -9 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-9+(n-1)(2) \\\\  & =-9+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2n-11 \\\\ 99 & =2n-11 \\\\ 110 & =2n \\\\ \\frac{110}{2} & =n \\\\ 55 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $99$ is the $55$th term of the sequence."} :step/id #uuid "ad138974-b0d6-561e-9544-cc96db0fdf17"}] :activity/title "Determining Indexes of Terms in Arithmetic Sequences" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571526}]}
